+# EXP-0007 — ARM RECORD: T04 on the repaired system
+
+Serves queue task **#55** (Fresh operational UIC benchmark on a functioning
+system), exit criteria **EXIT-4** / **EXIT-5**.
+
+This is the **arm half** of #55, recorded first-hand by the arm that ran it.
+It is **not** the UIC comparison: see *What this record does NOT establish*.
+
+Label discipline per `build-os/packets/routing/routing-gate.sh`: every number is
+marked **EXACT** (hook-counted / read from an artifact) or **UNAVAILABLE**. No
+figure is estimated into existence, and an unknown is recorded as `-`, never 0.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Arm identity
+
+| Field | Value | Tier |
+|---|---|---|
+| Arm | `exp0007-arm` (this session) | EXACT |
+| Host profile | `unknown_conservative` — Edit allowed, Bash approval_required, **no approver** | EXACT (matches #55 preflight) |
+| Task | T04 — fix 2 TypeScript errors (TS2322, TS2339) in `client/src/pages/UserDashboard.tsx` | EXACT |
+| Lane | `tiny` | EXACT |
+| Routing receipt | `routing-T04-userdashboard-typefix-20260809T143239Z.md` | EXACT |
+| selected_mode | `direct` | EXACT (selector verdict, `selector_note: -`) |
+| Task subagent dispatches | **0** (budget_max_subagents = 0 under `direct`) | EXACT |
+| Process (gate-chain) dispatches | **0** | EXACT |
+| Tokens / cost | `-` | **UNAVAILABLE** — interactive session; the gate's own label says tokens/cost are `unavailable_live`, close-time reconciliation only where headless |
+
+## 2. The headline finding — EXP-0005's failure does NOT reproduce
+
+EXP-0005 returned `gravito_system_harmful` with **0/12 accepted**, caused by
+`authority_bootstrap_permission_class_mismatch`: earning first mutation
+authority required **Bash**, which this host class gates behind an approval no
+approver can grant. Every arm therefore produced zero mutations.
+
+**On this arm the repair fired, and the arm mutated.** From
+`build-os/packets/routing/live_gate_log.tsv` (EXACT, hook-written):
+
+```
+14:32:05  none                       -       BLOCK-MUTATION-NO-RECEIPT   tool=Bash
+14:32:05  none                       -       RECOVERY-SELECTED           tool=Bash host=unknown_conservative source=selector
+14:32:15  none                       -       BLOCK-NO-RECEIPT            subagent_type=Explore
+14:32:35  none                       -       ROUTING-REQUEST-WRITE       tool=Write ungated=bootstrap-channel
+14:32:39  T04-userdashboard-typefix  -       BOOTSTRAP-RECEIPT-MINTED    via=routing-request-channel
+14:32:41  T04-userdashboard-typefix  direct  ALLOW-MUTATION              tool=Bash
+14:34:52  T04-userdashboard-typefix  direct  ALLOW-MUTATION              tool=Edit
+   … 4 further ALLOW-MUTATION tool=Edit through 14:35:17
+14:35:21  T04-userdashboard-typefix  direct  ALLOW-MUTATION              tool=Bash
+```
+
+The recovery selector chose the **no-shell** route for this host profile, the
+arm wrote `routing-request.json`, the hook redeemed it into an ordinary
+`route-task.sh` receipt from **inside the hook** — outside the tool-permission
+layer — and mutation authority was earned **in the same permission class as the
+work it authorizes** (Write/Edit). That is the stated invariant of the
+bootstrap channel, observed working in a live run rather than in a test.
+
+**Time cost of the bootstrap: 34 s** (14:32:05 → 14:32:39), 3 refused calls.
+EXACT. The larger 14:32:41 → 14:34:52 gap is **source reading, not gate
+overhead**, and is not charged to governance.
+
+## 3. Where the arm was actually blocked — and by whom
+
+The distinction matters for any harm verdict against the governance layer:
+
+| Attempt | Refused by | Count |
+|---|---|---|
+| `npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` | **Host permission layer** ("This command requires approval") | 2 (EXACT) |
+| `mcp__serena__get_diagnostics_for_file` | **Host permission layer** (permission not granted) | 2 (EXACT) |
+| Subagent dispatch (`Explore`) | Gravito routing gate, pre-receipt | 1 (EXACT) |
+| Subagent dispatch, post-receipt | Not attempted — `direct` records budget 0; dispatching would be silent escalation | 0 |
+
+**The routing gate ALLOWED both Bash calls** (rows 6 and 12 above). Both were
+then denied by the host. So on this arm the binding constraint on *verification*
+was the host permission layer, **not** Gravito. Gravito's only refusals were the
+three pre-receipt calls, all of which the bootstrap channel resolved in 34 s.
+
+This does not exonerate the governance layer in general — it is one arm, one
+task, one host profile — but it does mean a `gravito_system_harmful` verdict
+cannot be re-derived from this run's blocking pattern.
+
+## 4. Work product
+
+5 `Edit` mutations, one file, `client/src/pages/UserDashboard.tsx`:
+
+- **TS2322** — the `ApiKeyCard` prop type was hand-written as
+  `{ id: number; …; createdAt: Date; lastUsedAt: Date | null }`, but
+  `apiKeys.list` → `getApiKeysByUserId` is declared `Promise<Partial<ApiKey>[]>`
+  (`server/supabase-adapter.ts:158`) with **ISO-string** timestamps and every
+  field optional. Replaced with `Partial<ApiKey>` (type-only import) and the
+  optionality handled: `keyPrefix ?? ""`, `createdAt` guarded, `id` captured and
+  guarded so the `(id: number) => void` callbacks keep their strict signature.
+- **TS2339** — `invoice.date` does not exist; `subscription.billingHistory`
+  returns `BillingHistory[]`, whose field is `createdAt`
+  (`server/supabase-adapter.ts:104-114`). Corrected.
+
+No `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` / `@ts-nocheck`, no `any`, nothing deleted.
+
+**Acceptance status: UNVERIFIED-BY-COMPILER.** The verification command
+`npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json` could not be executed on this arm (§3). The
+fix is derived from the declared source types, not confirmed by a compiler run.
+Recording it as "accepted" would be exactly the synthetic activation this
